---
// Homepage body sections (below HomeHero). Uses Starlight's theme tokens so the
// site's light/dark toggle applies; wrapped in .not-content to opt out of the
// markdown typography rules (h2 underline, table header fill).
import VisitorMap from './VisitorMap.astro';
---

<div class="not-content mhs">
  <section class="mhs-band">
    <div class="mhs-split">
      <div>
        <p class="mhs-kicker">Calibrate a whole rig at once</p>
        <h2>From one recording to a full sensor model.</h2>
        <div class="mhs-prose">
          <p>MVIS is the calibration library behind the OpenMVIS benchmark. It solves camera intrinsics and distortion, extrinsics, time offsets, rolling-shutter readout, board poses and (optionally) the board shape, camera–IMU transforms, IMU intrinsics and biases in a single GTSAM factor graph.</p>
          <p>It reads ROS1 and ROS2 bags through <code>rosbags</code>, so ROS does not need to be installed. It also reads EuRoC/ASL folders, image folders and timestamped images.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <pre class="mhs-term" aria-label="Command-line usage"><span class="c"># cameras only</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>mvis cam -c camera.yaml

<span class="c"># cameras + IMUs, jointly</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>mvis cam-imu -c cam_imu.yaml

<span class="c"># apply the result and recalibrate; PASS / FAIL</span>
<span class="p">$ </span>mvis roundtrip -c cam_imu.yaml</pre>
        <p class="mhs-cap">One self-contained HTML report per run.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mhs-band">
    <p class="mhs-kicker">Not in Kalibr or Basalt</p>
    <h2>Six things the common tools do not do.</h2>
    <p class="mhs-lede">Kalibr and Basalt are the open-source camera–IMU toolboxes most people use. Neither covers these six cases. See the <a href="/getting-started/comparison/">full comparison</a>.</p>
    <ol class="mhs-gaps">
      <li>
        <h3>Rolling shutter + IMU</h3>
        <p>A rolling-shutter camera reads its rows one after another. MVIS solves that readout time together with the IMU. Kalibr's rolling-shutter tool is camera-only; Basalt has none.</p>
        <p class="mhs-gap-links"><a href="/guides/rolling-shutter/">Guide</a><a href="/why/rolling-shutter/">Why it matters</a></p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Global + rolling shutter + IMU</h3>
        <p>Global-shutter and rolling-shutter cameras on one rig, solved with all its IMUs in one run. Our VI-Rig recording has 2 global-shutter cameras, 2 rolling-shutter cameras and 4 IMUs.</p>
        <p class="mhs-gap-links"><a href="/benchmark/examples/virig-4imus-4cams/">Example</a><a href="/guides/rolling-shutter/#2-cameraimu-turn-readout-on-per-camera">Config</a></p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Board shape and pose</h3>
        <p>MVIS solves the board pose and, optionally, one height per corner (<code>estimate.board_points</code>). Kalibr and Basalt assume a flat board. On our VI-Rig mount, a flat solve biases the focal length by up to 1 % and the gyro scale by about 1 %.</p>
        <p class="mhs-gap-links"><a href="/why/board-shape/">Why it matters</a></p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Gyro-to-accel time offset</h3>
        <p><code>t_ga</code> is the time offset between an IMU's gyroscope and its accelerometer. MVIS fits it by default in camera–IMU runs. Kalibr and Basalt use one IMU clock, so the offset leaks into the camera time offset.</p>
        <p class="mhs-gap-links"><a href="/why/tga/">Why it matters</a></p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Digital-twin simulation</h3>
        <p>A digital twin is a simulated copy of your recording where the truth is known. MVIS re-solves it and reports the error of each parameter, so you can test the solver on your own rig.</p>
        <p class="mhs-gap-links"><a href="/guides/simulation/">Guide</a></p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Round-trip verification</h3>
        <p><code>mvis roundtrip</code> applies the calibration to its own data and calibrates again. It reports PASS or FAIL without ground truth, and exits non-zero on FAIL so it can run in CI.</p>
        <p class="mhs-gap-links"><a href="/guides/roundtrip/">Guide</a></p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="mhs-band">
    <p class="mhs-kicker">What the graph estimates</p>
    <h2>The state, not a sequence of stages.</h2>
    <div class="mhs-state">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Quantity</th><th scope="col">Symbol</th><th scope="col">Per</th><th scope="col">Unit</th><th scope="col">Notes</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="q">Intrinsics + distortion</td><td class="sym">f, c, k</td><td class="per">camera</td><td class="unit">px</td><td>Eight models, mixable within one rig</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">Camera–IMU extrinsics</td><td class="sym">T_CtoI</td><td class="per">camera</td><td class="unit">m · log(R) rad</td><td>Every camera to the base IMU, the reference IMU of the rig</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">Camera time offset</td><td class="sym">t_d</td><td class="per">camera</td><td class="unit">ms</td><td>About −123 ms of USB lag on the VI-Rig ELP stereo</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">Rolling-shutter readout</td><td class="sym">t_r</td><td class="per">camera</td><td class="unit">ms</td><td>Each corner projected at its own row time</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">IMU–IMU extrinsics</td><td class="sym">T_IstoI</td><td class="per">aux IMU</td><td class="unit">m · log(R) rad</td><td>Plus a per-IMU time offset</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">IMU intrinsics</td><td class="sym">D_w, D_a</td><td class="per">IMU</td><td class="unit">—</td><td><code>kalibr</code>, <code>rpng</code> or <code>calyx</code> convention</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">Gyro–accel offset</td><td class="sym">t_ga</td><td class="per">IMU</td><td class="unit">ms</td><td>About −5.7 ms on the T265 IMU; <a href="/why/tga/">why it matters</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">Biases</td><td class="sym">b_g, b_a</td><td class="per">IMU</td><td class="unit">rad/s · m/s²</td><td>Along the whole trajectory</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">Board pose + trajectory</td><td class="sym">T_BinW, T_ItoW(t)</td><td class="per">recording</td><td class="unit">m · log(R) rad</td><td>Chessboard, AprilGrid or ArUco targets</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="q">Board shape</td><td class="sym">z_k</td><td class="per">corner</td><td class="unit">mm</td><td>Optional, off by default; on for our VI-Rig runs; <a href="/why/board-shape/">why it matters</a></td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mhs-band">
    <div class="mhs-split">
      <div>
        <p class="mhs-kicker">Camera models</p>
        <h2>Eight projection models.</h2>
        <ul class="mhs-models">
          <li><code>radtan</code><span>Pinhole, radial–tangential</span></li>
          <li><code>kb4</code><span>Kannala–Brandt fisheye, the default; <a href="/why/kb4/">why</a></span></li>
          <li><code>equidistant</code><span>KB polynomial, under 90°</span></li>
          <li><code>fov</code><span>Field-of-view model</span></li>
          <li><code>double_sphere</code><span>Wide-angle fisheye</span></li>
          <li><code>eucm</code><span>Extended unified camera</span></li>
          <li><code>ucm</code><span>Unified camera</span></li>
          <li class="exp"><code>omni_radtan</code><span>Omnidirectional</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="mhs-kicker">Benchmark</p>
        <h2>Checked against Kalibr on TUM-VI.</h2>
        <div class="mhs-figs">
          <div class="mhs-fig"><b>0.2<small>px</small></b><p>largest median focal-length (fx, fy) difference from Kalibr; principal point within 0.35 px. Camera-only stereo, 8 raw recordings, view angles cut to 85° or less for every tool</p></div>
          <div class="mhs-fig"><b>&lt;0.1<small>mm</small></b><p>median stereo-baseline difference, inside the 0.1 mm run-to-run spread; same 8 recordings</p></div>
          <div class="mhs-fig"><b>1.8<small>mm</small></b><p>largest median lever-arm difference (camera position in the IMU frame), 4 raw and 4 512×512 recordings. Kalibr was given MVIS's intrinsics and baseline here</p></div>
          <div class="mhs-fig"><b>0.9<small>ms</small></b><p>median camera time offset above Kalibr's; Basalt is within 0.1 ms of Kalibr. MVIS also fits <code>t_ga</code> (−1.5 to −1.6 ms here), which Kalibr does not have</p></div>
        </div>
        <p class="mhs-cap">Benchmark batch 2026-11-10a. See the <a href="/benchmark/results/">Leaderboard</a> and each <a href="/devices/">device's calibration</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mhs-band">
    <div class="mhs-split">
      <figure class="mhs-rig">
        <img src="/media/hero/vi_rig.jpg" alt="The VI-Rig frame with its IMUs and cameras" width="1400" height="1050" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>VI-Rig, our own rig: up to 5 IMUs and 4 cameras across its recordings. They are in <a href="/datasets/">Datasets</a>.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <p class="mhs-kicker">It checks its own work</p>
        <h2>A low residual is not the test.</h2>
        <div class="mhs-prose">
          <p>A low reprojection error says a calibration fits its own data, not that it is right. In a round trip, PASS needs the IMU intrinsics and biases to collapse to identity and zero, and the geometry to hold. See <a href="/guides/roundtrip/">Round-trip validation</a>.</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="mhs-facts">
          <div><dt>Inputs</dt><dd>ROS1 and ROS2 bags, EuRoC/ASL folders, image folders, timestamped images</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Targets</dt><dd>AprilGrid, chessboard, ArUco</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Interop</dt><dd>Reads and writes Kalibr <code>camchain</code> and <code>camchain-imucam</code></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Export</dt><dd><code>mvis apply-calib</code> writes a copy of a raw ROS1 bag with the calibration applied</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mhs-band">
    <p class="mhs-kicker">Cite</p>
    <h2>If you use the toolbox or the benchmark.</h2>
    <div class="mhs-cites">
      <figure>
        <figcaption>Benchmark</figcaption>
        <pre class="mhs-term">@misc&#123;openmvis,
  title  = &#123;&#123;OpenMVIS&#125;: A Benchmark for Multi-Visual-Inertial Sensor Calibration&#125;,
  author = &#123;&#123;OpenMVIS Contributors&#125;&#125;,
  year   = &#123;2026&#125;,
  url    = &#123;https://openmvis.com&#125;
&#125;</pre>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <figcaption>Method</figcaption>
        <pre class="mhs-term">@article&#123;yang2024mvis,
  title   = &#123;Multi-visual-inertial system: Analysis, calibration, and estimation&#125;,
  author  = &#123;Yang, Yulin and Geneva, Patrick and Huang, Guoquan&#125;,
  journal = &#123;The International Journal of Robotics Research&#125;,
  year    = &#123;2024&#125;,
  volume  = &#123;43&#125;,
  number  = &#123;13&#125;,
  pages   = &#123;1995--2026&#125;,
  doi     = &#123;10.1177/02783649241245726&#125;
&#125;</pre>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="mhs-cap">Cite leaderboard results as <code>OpenMVIS leaderboard, batch 2026-11-10a</code>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mhs-band">
    <div class="mhs-split mhs-community">
      <div>
        <p class="mhs-kicker">Community</p>
        <h2>Bring your rig.</h2>
        <div class="mhs-prose">
          <p>OpenMVIS is open: the toolbox, the benchmark records and our own VI-Rig recordings. Add your device, your dataset or your results, or tell us where MVIS breaks.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="mhs-join">
          <li><a href="/contribute/submit-dataset/">Submit a dataset</a></li>
          <li><a href="/contribute/submit-results/">Submit results</a></li>
          <li><a href="/devices/">Device wiki</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://github.com/openmvis" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="mhs-visitors">
        <VisitorMap />
        <figcaption>Visitors to this page.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<style is:global>
  .mhs {
    --mhs-display: "Archivo", "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
    --mhs-mono: "JetBrains Mono", var(--sl-font-mono, ui-monospace), monospace;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .mhs code { font-family: var(--mhs-mono); font-size: 0.88em; }
  .mhs-band { padding-block: clamp(48px, 7vw, 88px); border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); }
  .mhs-band:first-child { border-top: 0; padding-top: clamp(32px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .mhs-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 var(--mhs-mono); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sl-color-accent); margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .mhs h2 { margin: 0; color: var(--sl-color-white); text-wrap: balance; font: 720 clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 42px)/1.05 var(--mhs-display); font-stretch: 112%; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .mhs-prose { max-width: 38rem; }
  .mhs .mhs-lede { max-width: 44rem; margin: 16px 0 0; }

  .mhs-gaps { list-style: none; counter-reset: gap; margin: 32px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0 28px; border-top: 2px solid var(--sl-color-white); }
  .mhs-gaps li { counter-increment: gap; margin: 0; padding: 18px 0 20px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-width: 0; }
  .mhs-gaps h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--sl-color-white); font: 650 18px/1.25 var(--mhs-display); font-stretch: 106%; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .mhs-gaps h3::before { content: counter(gap, decimal-leading-zero); display: block; font: 500 11px/1 var(--mhs-mono); letter-spacing: .12em; color: var(--sl-color-accent); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .mhs-gaps p { margin: 10px 0 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .mhs-gaps .mhs-gap-links { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 12px; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px 18px; font: 500 13px/1.4 var(--mhs-mono); }
  .mhs-gaps a, .mhs-lede a, .mhs-prose a, .mhs-cap a, .mhs-rig a, .mhs-state a, .mhs-models a { color: var(--sl-color-accent); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .mhs-lede a:hover, .mhs-gaps a:hover, .mhs-prose a:hover, .mhs-cap a:hover, .mhs-rig a:hover { color: var(--sl-color-accent-high); }
  .mhs-prose p { margin: 16px 0 0; }
  .mhs-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.05fr); gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 72px); align-items: start; }

  .mhs-term { background: #0f172a; color: #dbe4ee; border-radius: 10px; font: 400 14px/1.75 var(--mhs-mono); padding: 18px 20px; overflow-x: auto; margin: 0; border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); }
  .mhs-term .p { color: #38bdf8; user-select: none; }
  .mhs-term .c { color: #7d8ea4; }
  .mhs-cap { font: 500 12px/1.4 var(--mhs-mono); color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); margin: 10px 2px 0; }

  .mhs-state { margin-top: 36px; overflow-x: auto; border-top: 2px solid var(--sl-color-white); }
  .mhs-state table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; min-width: 640px; font-size: 15px; }
  .mhs-state th, .mhs-state td { text-align: left; padding: 13px 14px 13px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); vertical-align: baseline; background: none; }
  .mhs-state th { font: 500 11px/1 var(--mhs-mono); letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); padding-top: 14px; }
  .mhs-state td { color: var(--sl-color-gray-2); }
  .mhs-state td.q { color: var(--sl-color-white); font-weight: 500; }
  .mhs-state td.sym { font: 500 14px/1.3 var(--mhs-mono); color: var(--sl-color-accent); white-space: nowrap; }
  .mhs-state td.unit, .mhs-state td.per { font: 400 13px/1.3 var(--mhs-mono); color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); white-space: nowrap; }

  .mhs-models { list-style: none; margin: 28px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0 28px; }
  .mhs-models li { padding: 12px 0; margin: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); display: grid; gap: 3px; }
  .mhs-models code { font-size: 15px; color: var(--sl-color-white); font-weight: 500; }
  .mhs-models span { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  .mhs-models .exp code::after { content: "experimental"; margin-left: 8px; font: 500 10px/1 var(--mhs-mono); letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); border-radius: 4px; padding: 3px 5px; vertical-align: 2px; }

  .mhs-figs { margin-top: 28px; }
  .mhs-fig { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(7.5rem, auto) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 18px; align-items: baseline; padding: 16px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); }
  .mhs-fig b { font: 760 clamp(26px, 3vw, 36px)/1 var(--mhs-display); font-stretch: 115%; letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--sl-color-white); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .mhs-fig b small { font: 500 15px/1 var(--mhs-mono); color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); margin-left: 4px; letter-spacing: 0; }
  .mhs-fig p { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; }

  .mhs-rig { margin: 0; }
  .mhs-rig img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; max-width: 100%; border-radius: 10px; }
  .mhs-rig figcaption { font: 400 13px/1.5 var(--mhs-mono); color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); margin-top: 10px; }
  .mhs-facts { margin: 26px 0 0; }
  .mhs-facts div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 8.5rem minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 16px; padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); }
  .mhs-facts dt { font: 500 11px/1.9 var(--mhs-mono); letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  .mhs-facts dd { margin: 0; font-size: 15px; }

  .mhs-cites { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .mhs-cites figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  .mhs-cites figcaption { font: 500 12px/1 var(--mhs-mono); letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .mhs-cites .mhs-term { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.65; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .mhs-community { align-items: center; }
  .mhs-join { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 22px 0 0; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; }
  .mhs-join a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 40px; padding: 0 16px; border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline-shade, var(--sl-color-gray-5)); border-radius: 8px; color: var(--sl-color-white); text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; }
  .mhs-join a:hover { border-color: var(--sl-color-accent); color: var(--sl-color-accent); }
  .mhs-visitors { margin: 0; justify-self: center; width: min(100%, 320px); }
  .mhs .mhs-visitors .visitor-map { margin: 0; max-width: none; border-radius: 10px; overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline); }
  .mhs-visitors figcaption { font: 500 12px/1.4 var(--mhs-mono); color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); margin-top: 8px; text-align: center; }

  .mhs, .mhs-split > *, .mhs-cites > * { min-width: 0; max-width: 100%; }
  .mhs h2 { border-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: 0; }
  @media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .mhs-gaps { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .mhs-split, .mhs-cites { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .mhs-band { padding-block: 40px; }
    .mhs-term { font-size: 13px; }
    .mhs-state { position: relative; }
    .mhs-state::after { content: "scroll →"; position: sticky; left: 100%; display: block; width: max-content; margin-top: 6px;
                        font: 500 11px/1 var(--mhs-mono); color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .mhs-models, .mhs-gaps { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }
    .mhs-fig, .mhs-facts div { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 6px; }
  }
</style>
